{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And I saw</b> — Yefet said: that he was seeing in the visions of prophecy while he was in Shushan the capital, which is the kingdom of Persia, for from there the destroyer of Belshazzar's kingdom emerged, and it was as though he was by the Ulai River, perhaps like Ezekiel by the Chebar Canal, and אובל like יובל, 'and by the river he sends his roots' (as in Araba by streams of water), and the alef in place of yod, for ישי like אישי is also written with alef, and ויו\"ד תתימרו like with alef יתאמרו, and it was necessary to explain thus, for Daniel was in Babylon when King Belshazzar was killed. And Yefet said: it is the manner of a vision to say 'and behold'; only it is possible that Daniel went to Elam and returned in that year to Babylon."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The phrase 'והאל\"ף תחת יו\"ד' introduces a letter-substitution argument: alef standing in for yod. The quoted fragment 'ועל יובל ישלח שרשיו כערבים על יבלי מים' echoes Psalm 1:3 and Jeremiah 17:8 idiom; rendered literally as it merges biblical citation language with the argument about אובל/יובל."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:20:25.829626243Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}